    "presence": "present",
    "text": {
     "text": "You learned 様 is a \"formal name ender,\" but it can also mean manner. When you attach this to another noun with の and add に on the end to make it an adverb, you can describe something that's being done similarly to or in the same way as something else. In other words, something about it is just like that other thing — almost as if they were one and the same!",
